skill: "cap-table-modeler"
sections[3]:
  - "# cap-table-modeler\n\nModel funding-round scenarios against the live cap table: dilution per holder, ESOP pool top-ups and exit waterfalls. Use before a term sheet is signed, when an option grant changes the pool, or when the board asks what a down round does to founder and employee ownership. Produces scenarios, never decisions.\n\nOwner: role-cfo (pod-gna, executive). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"current cap table cap-table.toon (holders, classes, shares or units, price); term sheet parameters when available; ESOP policy esop-policy.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/cap-table-scenarios.toon with scenarios[] (pre-money, raise, pool top-up, per-holder dilution), exit waterfall[], and an approval block\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load cap-table.toon; verify the fully diluted share count reconciles with the last approved grant ledger, otherwise stop and flag the discrepancy.\n2. Record the scenario parameters exactly as stated by the operator (pre-money, raise amount, instrument); missing parameters are ask_question items.\n3. Model the new-money conversion and compute post-round ownership per holder with run_command; show dilution in percentage points, not only relative terms.\n4. Apply esop-policy.toon: compute the pool top-up needed to leave the target post-round option pool and attribute the dilution per policy (pre-money by default).\n5. Model the exit waterfall at three exit values (the term sheet valuation, half and double) with every liquidation preference, participation cap and conversion decision applied in order.\n6. Add the down-round case: the same round at half the pre-money, showing anti-dilution effects only if the instrument actually carries them.\n7. Sanity-check every scenario: post-round ownership sums to 100 percent and the waterfall fully distributes the exit value; a failed check blocks publication.\n8. Write cap-table-scenarios.toon with assumptions[] listing every input and its source; emit ask_question to role-cfo for scenario review before anything reaches the board.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nscenarios to role-cfo and board pack; approval recorded in scenarios.toon.\n"
